{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"virus component model virus component model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md","fileName":"Virus Component Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Virus Component Model","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 02:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Malware Types and Propagation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Malware Types and Propagation","Computer Virus","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"virus component model virus component model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md","fileName":"Virus Component Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Virus Component Model","heading":"Virus Component Model","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The virus component model separates a [[Computer Virus]] into an infection mechanism, a trigger, and a payload. The infection mechanism finds and modifies hosts, the trigger determines when another behavior begins, and the payload performs the intended effect.\n\nThis decomposition prevents replication from being mistaken for the virus's objective. Two viruses can use similar infection methods while carrying very different triggers and payloads, or share an effect while spreading differently.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Malware Types and Propagation","Computer Virus","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Virus Component Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","so